{
  "_doc": [
    "Registry of Kafka→Pulsar migration pairs the compare page scores in real time.",
    "Each entry tells the UI: when the user picks (busA,topicIdA) on one side and",
    "(busB,topicIdB) on the other side, the comparison is a known migration",
    "candidate; evaluate the listed `fields` against the live messages on both",
    "sides and surface a red/amber/green readiness indicator.",
    "",
    "Endpoint matchers (`topicIdContains` and `topicPathContains`) are *OR*'d in",
    "the UI engine — either substring hit qualifies the topic as a match.",
    "",
    "Severity model (lower = blocks migration sooner):",
    "  critical  — RCP business / correlation / filter input. Any gap is a STOP.",
    "  important — RCP mapping / enrichment. Gap is a WARN (RCP won't crash but",
    "              downstream consumers lose data).",
    "  info      — Optional / rarely populated. Informational only, never blocks.",
    "",
    "Field references in `rcpRef` are file:line citations into rcp-service/ as",
    "of 2026-05-15. See response/RCP-PULSAR-FIELD-MAP.md for the full audit."
  ],
  "version": 2,
